# TG-04 stage B: a new tg on a kept volume (make tg-upgrade), without making the volume
# again: tgd's own files (its api id and hash, TDLib's session) stay. On the console, which
# holds the volume's root: fetch writes the new package's two files over /packages/tg from
# the host (one guestfwd rule to a server of that directory only, @PORT@; the network is
# restrict=on), install --keep replaces tg and keeps its saved grant, and its page then
# lists only +sock. @KIB@ is the package's size, so a cut transfer is seen.
! panicked
! first process ended
! not fetched
! refused
< Type help to begin, or help tour.
< \r\n~>
> fetch --output /packages/tg/tg http://10.0.2.50:@PORT@/tg\r
limit 120 < \r\n~>
> fetch --output /packages/tg/tg.cmd http://10.0.2.50:@PORT@/tg.cmd\r
limit 60 < \r\n~>
> install --keep /packages/tg\r
limit 120 < tg (sha256 
< 2 files, @KIB@ KiB, command tg
< replaces tg (sha256 
< kept the saved grants: 
< tg installed with:
<   /data/home/tgd/window.sock  connect to
< \r\n~>
> programs tg\r
< saved grants:
^ \r\n  +sock /data/home/tgd/window.sock  /data/home/tgd/window.sock  connect to (saved)
^ \r\nrunning: none
< \r\n~>
x power off
> poweroff\r
